                        "entry_id": "a66e29c4-260a-3404-9272-f282a1ba3394",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A hoodlum or street thug, especially one from the townships; a township skollie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "South-Africa"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "45cb2f8a-99a8-426d-829f-a5d592521300",
                                "sense_id": "bd4f00fc-044a-3d0a-8893-8727f9032794",
                                "text": "A gang of tsotsis – hooligans – attacked a group of older men, and when the owner tried to throw them out they ran amok in the place, smashing everything in their way."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fcb64eec-d110-4c36-8570-49d846d22fb9",
                                "sense_id": "bd4f00fc-044a-3d0a-8893-8727f9032794",
                                "text": "Gangsters – known as tsotsis – carrying flick-knives or switchblades were plentiful and prominent [...]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a966e9c4-77c0-44e7-b04f-9e808e575ceb",
                                "sense_id": "bd4f00fc-044a-3d0a-8893-8727f9032794",
                                "text": "Mandela, standing up for all the tsotsis out there, said: \"Don't dismiss any youngsters who are not behaving according to your wishes.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
